Breaks: The rule an agent reads with every message drops the things mnemo cannot do for it: that the sender's name is claimed and not verified, that a sender nothing authorises is not authorised, that loading a project is not acting on the message, that a group message was not addressed to it in particular, and that a sender blocked on an answer has to be told the message arrived. An agent is left deciding whether a sender is authorised with no way to know what that field is worth.
Must fail: go test ./internal/criterion -run '^TestTheMailboxRuleSaysWhatCannotBeVerified$' -count=1

